.\" Keep CLI syntax aligned with src/main.rs and configuration with src/config.rs.
.\" Check hotkeys against src/keymap.rs, terminal-only handlers in src/tui.rs,
.\" and the controller's action availability before changing this reference.
.\" Keep this source ASCII and omit a release version to avoid stale metadata.
.TH YOUTA 1 "2026-10-07" "Youta" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
youta \- terminal audio player and subscription manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B youta
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL ]
.br
.B youta
.RI [ options ]
.B tui
.br
.B youta
.RI [ options ]
.B search
.RB [ \-\-channels ]
.I QUERY
.br
.B youta
.RI [ options ]
.RB { doctor | config | extractors }
.br
.B youta help
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Youta
plays audio, browses media sources, and keeps local subscriptions, playlists,
notes, listening history, and playback positions.
Running it without a command opens the terminal interface.
The default playback backend controls an invisible
.BR mpv (1)
process and uses
.BR yt-dlp (1)
for supported media resolution and downloads.
.PP
Available sources and actions depend on the features included in the build,
configured providers, installed helpers, and the selected item.
The contextual help opened with
.B ?
and the displayed action labels show the controls available in the current view.
YouTube subscriptions are managed locally; they do not synchronize with a
YouTube account.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Open the terminal player. Requires the
.B tui
build feature.
.TP
.BR search " [\-\-channels] " QUERY
Search YouTube videos, or channel names with
.BR \-\-channels .
Configure an official YouTube API key or an Invidious instance first;
the corresponding provider must be included in the build.
Results contain tab-separated identifiers, titles or names, and webpage URLs.
Quote queries containing spaces.
.TP
.B doctor
Check external helpers, configuration, storage, and tracker decoder support.
.TP
.B config
Print non-secret effective configuration and state paths.
.TP
.B extractors
List site extractors reported by the installed
.BR yt-dlp .
Requires the
.B yt-dlp
build feature.
.TP
.BR help " [COMMAND]"
Print general help or help for the named command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config-dir " PATH"
Use this application directory for configuration and state.
Overrides
.BR YOUTA_CONFIG_DIR .
This option is accepted before or after a subcommand.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Print the complete MIT license notice and exit.
This option is accepted before or after a subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print help. Use a subcommand followed by
.B \-\-help
for its options.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version.
.TP
.I URL
Open a complete HTTP or HTTPS page in the Web tab without starting playback.
The URL must not contain a username or password.
Quote URLs containing shell metacharacters.
A startup URL cannot be combined with a subcommand and requires both the
.B tui
and
.B web-browser
build features.
.SH TERMINAL HOTKEYS
Letter keys are case-sensitive:
.B s
and
.B S
are different commands.
.B Ctrl+
and
.B Alt+
mean holding that modifier while pressing the named key.
These bindings describe normal browsing unless a context is stated.
Popups, text editors, text-selection mode, and the keyboard pointer can consume
keys before normal browsing does.
For example, typing
.B q
in a search field inserts a letter, and arrow keys in an editor move its cursor.
.SS General navigation
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+B
Open the bug-report composer with title/body inputs and an enabled-by-default
With ASCII screenshot checkbox. See BUG REPORTS below.
.TP
.B ?
Open contextual help. Press
.B ?
or
.B Esc
to close it.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl+C
Quit from normal browsing. Popups can override or ignore these keys; close
the popup first if necessary.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Switch to the next or previous enabled top-level screen, wrapping at the ends.
.B Ctrl+Tab
and
.B Ctrl+Shift+Tab
also work when the terminal reports these combinations.
.TP
.BR j ", " k
Select the next or previous row.
.TP
.BR PageUp ", " PageDown
Move by the visible page in Local, Web, Subs, Radio, Apple Podcasts,
SoundCloud, archive.org, and LibriVox lists.
When Details has focus, scroll Details instead.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected source, folder, playlist, or item, or start its playback.
On the active Local media file, toggle pause like Space instead of reloading it.
In focused Details, an actionable selected link or media control can take
priority.
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " Alt+Left ", " Alt+Right
Go back, back, or forward in navigation, respectively.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the current popup or editor, leave focused Details, or return from a
supported nested view. In Local, open the parent directory when no higher
priority view consumes the key.
.TP
.B S
Open the Subs source root.
.TP
.B F2
Open downloaded media (Offline).
.TP
.B F3
Open Log when playback-history recording is enabled.
.TP
.B F4
Open playlists (Lists).
.TP
.B F5
Open listening statistics.
.TP
.BR p ", " F7
Open Preferences. Use
.B Up
and
.B Down
to focus a setting,
.B Space
to change it, and
.B Enter
to save. Press
.B Esc
or
.B p
to dismiss the dialog.
.TP
.B F9
Open project history. Press
.B F9
or
.B Esc
to close it.
.SS Playback and queue
.TP
.B Space
Toggle pause.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Seek backward or forward five seconds when seeking is available.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Left ", " Ctrl+Right
Seek backward or forward 20 seconds when seeking is available.
Editors and modal views retain their own key handling;
.B Alt+Left
and
.B Alt+Right
remain back and forward navigation.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Increase or decrease volume by five percentage points.
Use
.B j
and
.B k
to navigate ordinary lists.
.TP
.BR 0 " through " 9
Seek to 0 through 90 percent of the playing item when seeking is available.
.TP
.BR , " or " < "; " . " or " >
Decrease or increase playback speed by 0.1.
.TP
.BR [ ", " ]
Go to the previous or next chapter of seekable, non-live media.
.TP
.BR { ", " }
Play the previous or next queue item, using the source continuation where
available.
.TP
.B A
Toggle autoplay of the source list. Explicit queued items play first.
This preference is saved.
.TP
.B r
Toggle repeat of the playing item for this session.
In Local this key opens Rename when that feature is included; in Radio it
toggles recording. Live radio cannot repeat.
.TP
.B a
Add the selected playable item to the queue.
At the Subs source root this key opens Add RSS feed instead.
.TP
.B Ctrl+n
Put the selected playable item next in the queue.
.TP
.B u
Open the playback queue. Within it,
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
select an entry,
.B Enter
plays it,
.B x
or
.B Delete
removes it, and
.B C
clears the queue.
.B Esc
or
.B u
closes the queue.
.TP
.B w
Toggle a waveform for supported local audio or video using
.BR ffmpeg .
.TP
.B F10
Open the ASCII audio visualizer while playback is loaded, when the feature
and its helper are available.
.B Esc
or
.B F10
closes it.
.SS Search, subscriptions, and Web
.TP
.B /
Begin a search in the current source or edit the address in Web.
While editing,
.B Enter
submits,
.B Esc
cancels,
.B Left/Right
move the cursor,
.B Backspace
deletes the preceding character, and
.B Ctrl+w
deletes the preceding word.
.TP
.B v
Switch between videos and channels in YouTube search.
In Yandex Music, cycle the search category.
.TP
.B N
Toggle relevance or newest-first ordering in YouTube search.
.TP
.B C
Toggle the Creative Commons filter in YouTube video search.
An active download takes priority: this key cancels that download instead.
.TP
.B c
Open the selected item's channel or source when supported.
.TP
.B s
Subscribe locally to the selected YouTube channel, including an unsubscribed
channel identified by a video result.
On an already subscribed channel, open an unsubscribe confirmation;
.B Enter
confirms and
.B Esc
cancels. Downloaded files are kept.
.TP
.B a
At the Subs source root, open Add RSS feed.
Enter an HTTP or HTTPS RSS/Atom feed URL and press
.B Enter
to save, or
.B Esc
to cancel.
.TP
.B R
Refresh Web or the active subscription's videos or episodes.
In Yandex Music recommendations, this key downloads twenty recommendations
when that action is available.
.TP
.B h
Toggle YouTube Shorts in YT search results or an active YouTube subscription's
item list. Both use the same saved preference. Explicit video URLs remain
available even when Shorts are hidden.
.TP
.B i
Toggle item Details in the split Subs layout.
.TP
.B X
Toggle automatic downloads for an eligible YouTube channel.
In Yandex Music, dislike or undo dislike of the selected track.
.TP
.B D
Review a full-channel YouTube download when available.
In an open Yandex Music album, download the album.
.PP
In archive.org items, ZIP files are folders after the direct tracks.
.B Enter
opens a ZIP's audio member list and then plays the selected member.
.B Esc
returns to the parent item, selecting the same ZIP.
Member paths remain visible; the whole ZIP is not downloaded or extracted locally.
Nested archives are not opened, and member seeking depends on the remote service.
.SS Downloads, playlists, and notes
.TP
.B Insert
Toggle the download mark on a supported playable row.
.TP
.B d
Download the marked items or selected supported media.
When a download-choice dialog opens, use
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
to choose,
.B Enter
to confirm, and
.B Esc
to cancel.
.TP
.B Ctrl+d
Open the persistent download queue. Use
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
to select,
.B r
to retry,
.B x
or
.B Delete
to cancel or remove an entry, and
.B Esc
to close.
.TP
.B l
Toggle the selected supported item's membership in the built-in todo playlist.
.TP
.B P
Open the playlist picker for the selected supported item.
Use
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
to select,
.B Enter
to toggle membership,
.B n
to create a playlist, and
.B Esc
to close.
In the name-and-description editor,
.B Tab
switches fields and
.B Enter
saves.
.TP
.B e
Edit the selected playlist's name and description in the Lists index.
.TP
.B n
Add or edit a private note for the selected supported target, including Local
folders. The Add private note / Edit private note row in Details opens the same
editor. Local folders are source targets identified by their exact full path,
separate from notes on child files; selecting
.B ..
targets the parent folder. Folder notes use the existing note storage.
Inside the editor,
.B Enter
inserts a newline,
.B Ctrl+s
saves,
.B Delete
requests deletion, and
.B Esc
closes. Confirm deletion with
.B Enter
or a second
.BR Delete .
.SS Local files and Radio
.TP
.B :
Enter a Bash command for the selected Local file or folder in the seek-bar area.
The default-on
.B cmd
build feature requires Bash and a Unix terminal; commands are unavailable in
the GUI and inside read-only archive folders.
.B Enter
runs the command in the displayed directory with terminal input and output;
.B Esc
cancels before execution.
.B Ctrl+C
interrupts the command. After it finishes, any key returns to Youta and
refreshes the directory. Commands run with your permissions and may modify
or delete files;
they are not sandboxed. Bash startup files are not loaded.
.IP
Use an unquoted
.B %
argument for the full selected path, safely passed as one argument, or
.B %.mp3
to append a suffix. Quoted and escaped percent signs remain literal.
For substitutions, arithmetic, grouping, and other complex Bash syntax, use
.B \(dq$1\(dq
instead of the percent shortcut: the selected path is Bash's first positional
parameter. Changing positional parameters changes $1 but not the percent
shortcut.
.IP
While entering a command,
.B Tab
completes command names from PATH and Bash builtins, or filenames relative to
the displayed directory. Absolute paths and ~/ are also supported. The first
Tab inserts a common prefix; repeated Tab cycles matches. Spaces and quotes
are quoted automatically. Completion neither executes shell expansions nor
loads programmable Bash completion scripts.
.B Up/Down
recall previous commands and restore the unsent draft past the newest entry.
.B Ctrl+R
opens the ten newest matching commands. Type a case-sensitive substring,
select with
.BR Up/Down ,
and press
.B Enter
to execute against the current selection, or
.B Esc
to close history search.
.IP
The standalone Cargo feature and Gentoo USE flag are both named
.BR cmd .
Omit cmd from an explicit Cargo
.B \-\-no-default-features
build or use Gentoo
.B USE=\(dq\-cmd\(dq
to remove command support.
.TP
.B r
Rename the selected Local entry when supported.
.TP
.B c
Open Copy for selected Local files or folders when supported.
The source is retained. Use
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
to select a destination folder and
.B Enter
to open it. Confirm copying into the displayed directory with
.B c
or
.BR C .
.TP
.B m
Open Move for selected Local entries when supported.
In the destination picker,
.B j/k
or
.B Up/Down
select a directory,
.B Enter
opens it, and
.B m/M
confirms moving into the current directory.
.B Esc
cancels either destination picker before transfer starts.
During Copy or Move, the foreground dialog blocks navigation and dismissal
until completion and displays byte or entry progress when available.
Folder listings and transfer progress wake the terminal UI when ready,
without waiting for a periodic response check.
.TP
.BR Shift+j ", " Shift+k
Extend Local file/folder selection down or up for copy, move, or quality analysis,
when supported and reported distinctly by the terminal.
.TP
.B Delete
Request Move to Trash for selected Local entries when supported.
Confirm with
.B Enter
or cancel with
.BR Esc .
.TP
.B x
Request Move to Trash for selected downloaded media in Offline.
.TP
.B H
Toggle showing all Local files.
.TP
.B Z
Cycle Local folder-size sorting off, ascending, and descending when folder
size measurement is enabled.
.PP
Preferences includes
.B Natural Local filename sorting (1, 2, 10)
to order numbered files and folders numerically, including inside local archives.
It is off by default. Folders stay first unless size sorting is active;
equal sizes use the selected filename order. Saving keeps the same entry selected.
The configuration key is
.BR ui.natural_local_sort .
.TP
.B f
Fingerprint selected supported Local audio through Chromaprint and AcoustID.
In Radio, toggle the selected station's favorite status.
.TP
.B V
Analyze supported Local audio quality for the selected item or marked files
and folders.
.TP
.B B
Cycle Radio sorting.
.TP
.B r
Start or stop recording in Radio.
.PP
Rename, Move, and Trash are unavailable inside read-only archives.
.SS Details, links, and optional actions
YouTube description hashtags are inline links. Activating one searches
YouTube for that hashtag inside Youta. Select it with the Details-link keys
below or click it with the mouse.
Use
.B Alt+Left
or
.B Backspace
to return to the previous view with its search results, selected item, and
Details scroll position, without repeating the search or interrupting playback.
.PP
Email addresses in Details descriptions and public comments are clickable.
They open the system's default mail application with one recipient; Youta does
not send mail. Details emails also support the link-selection keys below.
External email actions are unavailable on Linux virtual consoles without a
desktop opener.
.TP
.BR Alt+Up ", " Alt+Down ", " Alt+u ", " Alt+d
Scroll visible Details one line up or down.
.B Alt+u/d
also work on Linux virtual consoles whose keymaps intercept Alt-arrow keys.
.TP
.BR Alt+j ", " Alt+k
Select the next or previous Details link, or an expanded Wikidata media
control when those controls have focus.
.TP
.BR Alt+Home ", " Alt+End
Select the first or last Details link.
.TP
.B Alt+Enter
Activate the selected Details link.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
Scroll to the beginning or end when Details has focus.
.TP
.B t
Enter or leave Details text-selection mode for copying through the terminal.
.B Esc
also leaves this mode.
.TP
.B T
Toggle chapter timestamps.
.TP
.B W
Expand or collapse statements for an available Wikidata link.
.TP
.BR o ", " O
Open the selected item's webpage or its channel's webpage in the external
browser. In Radio both keys open the station page.
External browser actions require an available graphical opener.
.TP
.B y
Copy the selected item's link.
.TP
.B F6
Open available public comments or reviews.
.B F6
or
.B Esc
closes the popup.
.TP
.B G
Generate a video summary when the configured summary backend and selected
item support it.
.TP
.B Y
Open available YouTube captions.
.TP
.B Q
Show a QR code for the selected YouTube video when supported.
.B Q
or
.B Esc
closes it.
.TP
.BR I ", " M ", " U ", " E
Open the selected item's Internet Archive upload, Amazon S3 upload,
Wikimedia Commons upload, or Evernote note review, respectively, when the
corresponding integration and item are available.
Review the destination and fields before submitting.
.B I
supports YouTube videos and eligible Local media files when the
.B archive-upload
feature is built; this feature is independent of archive.org browsing.
Local private paths are omitted from public upload metadata.
Audio is prepared as Opus; eligible Local video can instead use stream-copy MKV.
Folders and unavailable selections cannot start publication.
.TP
.BR L ", " g ", " b
In Yandex Music, like or undo like of a track, open its artist, or open its
album, respectively, when available.
.TP
.B F11
Start sharing the selected Local file or folder over the LAN when supported.
.TP
.B F12
Share a podcast feed for selected Local audio or an eligible YouTube channel
when supported. Selecting a playable Local file or a YouTube channel opens
feed options first; selecting a Local folder starts sharing directly.
In the active LAN-share popup,
.B x
stops sharing;
.B Esc
only closes the popup.
.SS Keyboard pointer
.B F8
toggles the terminal keyboard pointer.
While active, arrow keys move it one cell,
.B Enter
clicks, and
.B Esc
or
.B F8
exits pointer mode.
.SH BUG REPORTS
Press
.B Ctrl+Alt+B
to compose a public GitHub issue without leaving Youta.
The optional text screenshot captures the visible screen before the form opens,
preserves Unicode titles, and omits artwork and terminal-image commands.
In the GUI it is a labeled text snapshot, not a raster image.
Private-note and credential editors suppress capture. Common credentials and
home paths are redacted; large screenshots are truncated. Other visible
personal text may remain: uncheck With ASCII screenshot to exclude it.
.PP
.B Tab
and
.B Shift+Tab
move between fields;
.B Space
toggles the screenshot checkbox when selected.
.B Enter
in the body inserts a newline.
.B Ctrl+S
or Submit sends directly, with no additional review or confirmation screen.
.B Ctrl+Enter
also submits on terminals that can distinguish it from plain Enter.
While sending, Submit is gray and disabled, a simple spinner animates,
and editing, dismissal, and repeated submission are blocked.
An explicit failure allows retrying; an uncertain outcome asks you to check the
issue list to avoid duplicates.
.B Esc
closes the form when it is not sending.
.PP
The report ends automatically with a separator, Youta version, and OS.
Drafts and screenshots are kept only in memory.
Submission uses an installed, authenticated
.BR gh (1)
and works from a physical TTY without opening a browser.
The body is sent through standard input, not a browser URL.
Missing-helper and authentication errors include guidance; Copy is also
available. Never include authentication tokens in a report.
.PP
.UR https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_auth_login
GitHub CLI authentication, including headless token input
.UE
.br
.UR https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_issue_create
GitHub CLI issue creation
.UE
.SH AUDIO CACHE
On Linux, the default
.B cache
build feature retains fetched, validated HTTP audio bytes in RAM across track
switches. Returning to cached YouTube audio can skip extraction and reuse the
saved playback position, including after playing several other tracks.
Uncached or evicted ranges still need the network; the decoder still opens
when returning to a track. Audio is fetched on demand, not downloaded in full
automatically.
.PP
The cache observes a best-effort ceiling of 90% total memory usage, respecting
both available physical memory and tighter container limits. Older bytes are
evicted under pressure. This does not allocate 90% of RAM to Youta or prevent
other applications from exceeding the threshold. Missing memory measurements
disable retention. Audio bytes and resolved URLs are session-only.
.PP
Live streams, HLS/DASH manifests, unsupported HTTP servers, configured HTTP
proxies, and platforms without memory measurements use ordinary playback.
Archive.org's existing exact-original download cache remains available.
Omit the
.B cache
Cargo feature, or use Gentoo
.BR USE="-cache" ,
to remove RAM audio caching from both frontends.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On Linux the default application directory is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/youta ,
or
.I ~/.config/youta
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
Other platforms use their platform configuration directory.
Select another directory with
.B YOUTA_CONFIG_DIR
or, at higher priority,
.BR \-\-config-dir .
.PP
Settings load in increasing priority: built-in defaults,
.IR config.toml ,
.IR secrets/credentials.toml ,
and environment variables beginning with
.BR YOUTA_ .
Two underscores express nested keys: for example,
.B YOUTA_PLAYBACK__VOLUME_PERCENT=40
sets
.BR playback.volume_percent .
The repository's
.I config.example.toml
documents available settings.
.PP
The first unconfigured YouTube search in the terminal offers provider setup.
It saves API keys in
.I secrets/credentials.toml
and the Invidious instance URL in
.IR config.toml .
Stored credentials are plaintext; Youta creates private directories and files
with user-only permissions on Unix.
Preferences also exposes provider setup when the build supports it.
.SH FILES
The following paths are relative to the selected application directory.
.TP
.I config.toml
User settings.
.TP
.I secrets/credentials.toml
Provider credentials.
.TP
.I subscriptions.opml
Portable local subscriptions to RSS, podcast, and compatible channel feeds.
.TP
.I cmd-log
Plaintext Local command history: the latest 100 submitted commands,
one per line,
up to 8192 bytes each. Requires the cmd feature. Delete while Youta is closed to
clear it. Written with owner-only Unix permissions; included in configuration
Git synchronization. Commands may contain passwords or tokens. Command text is
excluded from diagnostics and bug-report screenshots.
.TP
.I state/*.toml
Canonical progress, history, notes, bookmarks, statistics, playlists, and
move-journal documents for the default files backend.
Close Youta before editing these documents.
.TP
.I state/.lock
The files backend's exclusive instance lock. Only one process can open that
backend in an application directory at a time.
.TP
.I runtime/
Restart session state and playback checkpoints.
.TP
.I cache/
Regenerable search, metadata, and local archive caches.
.TP
.I thumbnail-cache/
Persistent artwork cache.
.TP
.I downloads/
Downloaded media and related data.
.TP
.I state.sqlite3
State database when the optional SQLite backend is selected and compiled in.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YOUTA_CONFIG_DIR
Select the application directory unless
.B \-\-config-dir
is supplied.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Select the Linux configuration base directory.
.TP
.B YOUTA_<SECTION>__<KEY>
Override a nested setting, for example
.B YOUTA_UI__THEME=dark
or
.BR YOUTA_PLAYBACK__AUTOPLAY=true .
Environment overrides take precedence over saved preferences.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the terminal player:
.PP
.nf
.B youta
.fi
.PP
Open a Web directory without starting playback:
.PP
.nf
.B youta \(aqhttps://example.com/music/\(aq
.fi
.PP
Search configured YouTube metadata:
.PP
.nf
.B youta search \(aqambient music\(aq
.B youta search \-\-channels \(aqradio\(aq
.fi
.PP
Inspect a separate application directory:
.PP
.nf
.B youta \-\-config-dir /path/to/youta config
.B youta \-\-config-dir /path/to/youta doctor
.fi
.PP
Start with a volume override:
.PP
.nf
.B YOUTA_PLAYBACK__VOLUME_PERCENT=40 youta
.fi
